# Sizes and paint order from docs/design/primitives/z-stack.md: `status` under `OK` is 6x1 and
# reads `OKatus`, the later layer is the one that shows, and an empty ZStack is 0x0. `a` steps
# the alignment of `Go` in its 8x3 backdrop, `s` swaps the source order of the two blocks, and
# `g` adds an `if` group of layers.
app zstack
size desktop

expect node type=ZStack nth=0 frame 0,3,6x1
expect node type=Text text="atus" frame 0,3,6x1
expect node layout=_FrameLayout nth=0 frame 0,3,2x1
expect node type=ZStack nth=1 frame 9,3,8x3
expect node type=ZStack nth=2 frame 20,3,4x2
expect node type=ZStack nth=3 frame 1,7,0x0
expect text 3 "OKatus   Go······   bbAA"
expect node type=ZStack nth=5 frame 17,7,4x1
expect node id=abcd frame 17,7,4x1
expect node id=ef frame 17,7,2x1
expect text 7 "[]     B         efcd    base"
check
shot desktop

# Centred in 8x3, `Go` has three cells on each side and one row above it.
type "aaaa"
expect node type=Text text="Go" frame 12,4,2x1
expect text 9 "alignment center, bb on top"

# Swapped, the block `AAAA` is the later layer and covers `bb`.
type "s"
expect text 3 "OKatus   ········   AAAA"
expect text 4 "         ···Go···   AAAA"
shot swapped-center
check

# A `ForEach` and an `if` build layers too. The items `abcd` and `ef` share one frame under the
# ZStack, so `ef` covers the start of `abcd`; `g` adds an `if` group whose `g` and `h` sit on
# `base`'s first cell, and the later one shows. `siblings-disjoint` looks through the list to
# the ZStack, so the bare `check` passes.
type "g"
expect text 7 "[]     B         efcd    hase"
expect node type=Text text="h" frame 25,7,1x1
check
shot grouped
